sequenceDiagram
  participant B as Browser
  participant A as App / coordinator
  participant D as SQLite
  participant Q as Qwen worker
  participant F as FLUX worker
  B->>B: Persist request key in sessionStorage
  B->>A: POST URL + key; cookie + CSRF
  A->>D: Check owner + exact-key replay
  alt Exact replay
    D-->>A: Original selection + immutable expiry
    A-->>B: Existing view; no new admission / generation
  else Fresh key
    A->>A: Validate destination + bounded RSS / Atom fetch
    Note over B,A: RSS rejection stays on form; no inference
    A->>D: Atomically save snapshot + reserve quotas + admit
    A-->>B: Validated view; original one-hour expiry
    B->>B: Save validated response, then navigate
    Note over A,F: For each admitted story; app orchestrates both stages
    A->>D: Persist Qwen invocation + submitting state
    A->>Q: Submit fixed /run job
    Q-->>A: Provider job ID
    A->>D: Persist provider job ID
    loop Existing job
      A->>Q: Poll /status/id
    end
    Q-->>A: Prompt + measured usage
    A->>A: Verify output; compose + filter final prompt
    A->>D: Save final prompt; persist FLUX intent + submitting state
    A->>F: Submit fixed /run job
    F-->>A: Provider job ID
    A->>D: Persist provider job ID
    loop Existing job
      A->>F: Poll /status/id
    end
    F-->>A: Image + measured usage
    A->>D: Verify image; settle attempts; save metadata only
  end
  B->>A: Read-only owned batch / existing image request
  opt Existing result retrieval required
    A->>F: Retrieve existing job result; never regenerate
    F-->>A: Temporary retained output, if available
  end
  A-->>B: Validated image bytes, if available
  B->>B: Decode; commit IndexedDB Blob until original view expiry
  Note over B,A: Reload never automatically retries uncertain POST; explicit retry uses same key
  Note over A,F: Unknown provider acceptance / execution: hold reservations; freeze new dispatch<br/>Poll known IDs when possible; operator reconciliation; no automatic replay
  Note over B,F: Provider output is temporary. SQLite stores metadata; no permanent image archive.
